{"The new optimized paginator explicitly slices querysets using negative start offsets when enable_advanced_features is set, and BasePaginator now conditionally permits negative offsets for prev cursors, contradicting other paginator implementations that treat negative offsets as invalid, leading to inconsistent behavior and potential runtime errors": 0.892361044883728, "OptimizedCursorPaginator.get_item_key applies math.floor/ceil directly to the ordered field value, but OrganizationAuditLogsEndpoint orders by datetime, causing a TypeError and breaking pagination when the optimized paginator is selected": 0.9736135005950928, "OrganizationAuditLogsEndpoint enables the optimized paginator for any member with has_global_access, but that flag defaults to True for OrganizationMember, making the feature broadly available rather than restricted to administrators as intended": 0.513834536075592}